Caroline and I co-organized the mini-symposium [“Manifold learning, trajectory inference, and applications in biology”](https://meetings.siam.org/sess/dsp_programsess.cfm?SESSIONCODE=80578). Caroline's talk “Trajectory inference in Wasserstein space” was featured in [SIAM news](https://www.siam.org/publications/siam-news/articles/novel-algorithm-infers-particle-trajectories-in-cell-point-clouds/).
We had a great time at this conference (check out some pictures [here](https://tarheels.live/cmoosm/2024/11/01/siam-news-on-carolines-talk-at-mds-24/)).

I also gave a presentation in the mini-symposium [“Incorporating Optimal Transport in Machine Learning: Theory and Applications”](https://meetings.siam.org/sess/dsp_programsess.cfm?SESSIONCODE=80594) and presented a poster in the mini-symposium [“Computational Methods for Measure Transport and Generative Modeling”](https://meetings.siam.org/sess/dsp_programsess.cfm?SESSIONCODE=80634).
